---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About: A Young Nurse's Illustrated Primer">
  <div class="column">
    <h1>About this book</h1>
    <h2>What it is, and what it isn't</h2>
    <p>
      This book teaches how modern AI works by having you build a telephone-triage nurse, step by step. It is not
      medical advice, and the machines you build in it are not safe to triage anyone. The messages in it are
      made up. No real patient data is used anywhere.
    </p>
    <h2>How it was written</h2>
    <p>
      Drafts of the prose were written with AI help (Claude, made by Anthropic). Any chapter that has not yet had a
      human edit says so at the top, as does any chapter whose medical content a clinician has not yet reviewed.
    </p>
    <p><code>TODO(review)</code> Name the human editor and the clinical reviewers here once they have signed off.</p>
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p>
      Every chapter lists its sources at the end. The book cites primary sources only, and a check runs on every
      build to make sure each source is cited and each citation has a source.
    </p>
    <h2>Edition</h2>
    <p>This is edition <span data-version>{__PRIMER_VERSION__}</span>. Every page shows the same edition stamp.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
